# NOTE: www -> apex redirect is NOT handled here.
# Cloudflare Pages _redirects only match on the request PATH, never the
# hostname, so a rule like "https://www.yevilla.com/* ..." silently never
# fires (www was being served as a 200 duplicate). The www -> yevilla.com
# 301 is configured as a zone-level Single Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare
# dashboard (Rules -> Redirect Rules):
#   When:  http.host eq "www.yevilla.com"
#   Then:  301 -> concat("https://yevilla.com", http.request.uri.path)
